WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.690
You ask Noor about file formats.

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:05.930
She says: I think format B works.

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:07.090
Not tested.

00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:09.360
Then someone tidies the note.

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:12.320
By Friday, it’s in the release notes.

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:13.410
In bold.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:22.150
The task gets marked done, because the message arrived.

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:26.260
Good Teammate keeps the fine print attached.

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:30.590
First, it finds who should answer.

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:32.550
A fact, you look up.

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:34.730
A judgment goes to the expert.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.890
A choice goes to the owner.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:42.030
Then it drafts one bounded request, and leaves the doubt in.

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:47.060
You gave it no permission to send.

00:00:47.430 --> 00:00:50.560
So the card says: drafted, not sent.

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:00.890
Good Teammate.

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:02.430
Get the right help.

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:04.330
Keep the meaning intact.
